---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Policy - How TDEE Check Content Is Reviewed"
  description="How TDEE Check creates and reviews its health content: published formulas, dietitian review by Farah Akram, accuracy checks, corrections and advertising separation."
  path="/editorial-policy/"
  crumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Editorial Policy', path: '/editorial-policy/' },
  ]}
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pt-10">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-ink-900">Editorial policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm font-semibold text-ink-500">Last updated: October 2026</p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink-900">Who reviews our content</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
      Every calculator and guide on TDEE Check is reviewed before publication by
      <strong>Farah Akram, Dietitian</strong>, who checks the formulas, the safety limits, and the wording of the health
      guidance. You can find her on
      <a class="font-bold text-brand-700 underline" href="https://www.instagram.com/dietitian_faraa" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Instagram</a> and
      <a class="font-bold text-brand-700 underline" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/farah-akram-41b572429" rel="noopener" target="_blank">LinkedIn</a>.
      Pages name their reviewer so readers always know whose judgment stands behind the numbers.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink-900">Where our formulas come from</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
      We only use published, widely validated methods, and each calculator page names its formula: the Mifflin-St Jeor
      equation (1990) for BMR and TDEE, the Katch-McArdle equation when body fat percentage is known, the Boer and James
      equations for lean body mass, the US Army circumference method for body fat percentage, and the World Health
      Organization categories for BMI. We do not publish proprietary or invented formulas.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink-900">How we check accuracy</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-6">
      <li>Every worked example in our guides is calculated by hand and compared with the calculator output before publication.</li>
      <li>Result ranges and safety floors are stated on each page, including the general floors of 1,200 kcal per day for women and 1,500 kcal per day for men.</li>
      <li>When a formula or guideline is updated by its source, the affected pages are updated and the change noted.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink-900">Corrections</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
      If you spot an error in a result, a formula, or a guide, tell us through the
      <a class="font-bold text-brand-700 underline" href="/contact/">contact page</a>. Verified corrections are made
      promptly and visibly, and the page date is updated. Reader reports are one of the ways this site stays accurate.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink-900">Advertising and independence</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
      This site is supported by advertising, including Google AdSense. Advertisements are labeled as advertisements and
      are kept visually separate from calculator results and editorial content. Advertisers have no influence on our
      formulas, our results, or our guidance, and no result on this site can be bought or changed by a sponsor.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink-900">A note on drafting</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
      Drafts for this site may be prepared with research and writing tools, but nothing is published until it has passed
      the dietitian review described above and the accuracy checks on this page. The responsibility for every number on
      TDEE Check is human, and it sits with our reviewer.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
